[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 2, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008311-cloud-itonami-isco-8311-locomotive-drivers-coverage" "adr-2799005413-cloud-itonami-isco-5413-prison-guards-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["throw the track switch" "threw the track switch" "throw the switch" "thrown the switch" "clear the signal" "cleared the signal" "set the track route" "set the route" "route the train" "routed the train" "finalize the track routing" "finalized the track routing" "activate the signal" "activated the signal" "change the signal aspect" "change the signal indication" "actuate the track switch" "actuated the switch"], :adr/id 2799008312, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-service-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-maintenance-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-service-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-maintenance-order}, :auto #{:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}", :actor/domain :transport/rail-signal-crew-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-maintenance-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-operator :no-actuation :op-not-allowed :unknown-section :section-wrong-operator :finalizes-switch-or-signal], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "8312", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799008312: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8312 Railway Brake, Signal and Switch Operators administrative/logistics scheduling coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8312\n-- Railway Brake, Signal and Switch Operators** only.\n\nThis is a retry batch (8 sibling agents dispatched together this\nsession, some retrying repos that already existed from an earlier\nrate-limited attempt). For ISCO 8312 specifically, `gh api\nrepos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8312` returned a clean 404\nbefore any work began -- this was genuinely a fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8312\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8312\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Railway Brake, Signal and Switch\nOperators\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`. This\nADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8312` entry to\n`:implemented`. `kotoba.occupation.wave/wave-of \"8312\"` resolves to\nwave 2 (`coordination-logistics`, sub-major `83`), consistent with this\nactor's administrative/logistics-scheduling framing.\n\n**Rail-signal/switch-operation safety dimension.** Railway Brake,\nSignal and Switch Operators directly control track switches and\nsignaling in the real occupation -- errors in that physical work can\ncause train collisions or derailments. This actor does NOT model that\nphysical authority. It is deliberately restricted to ADMINISTRATIVE and\nLOGISTICS SCHEDULING coordination around the occupation (inspection/\nstatus-record logging, crew-roster scheduling, safety-concern\nescalation, and maintenance-order procurement coordination for\nswitch/signal equipment) -- never the switch-throw, signal-clearance or\ntrack-routing decision itself. The closed proposal-op allowlist\nstructurally excludes any op that could directly finalize such a\ndecision, and the governor independently, permanently hard-blocks any\nproposal whose free-text action description names such a finalization\naction, regardless of the declared `:op` or confidence -- this is not\nan escalation path a human can approve through, it is an outright,\nstructural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set), independently\nre-cloned and read in full this session. Sibling ISCO-08 sub-major-83\nactors built in the same fleet session --\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8311`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8311)\n(Locomotive Engine Drivers) -- independently converged on the same\nproposal-op vocabulary (`:log-service-record`,\n`:schedule-crew-operation`, `:flag-safety-concern`,\n`:coordinate-maintenance-order`) from the same task template, which\nthis ADR treats as confirmation of a stable pattern for this domain\nrather than coincidence.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8312` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for railway brake, signal\nand switch operators, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as\nevery prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Rail Signal\nCrew Advisor ⊣ RailSignalCrewGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **administrative/logistics scheduling\ncoordination ONLY, never switch/signal operation authority** -- it must\nNEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising a switch-throw, signal-clearance, or track-routing decision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-service-record` -- switch/signal inspection and status data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- operator-roster/shift scheduling\n  proposal only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a switch-malfunction/signal-anomaly\n  concern, ALWAYS escalates immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-maintenance-order` -- signal/switch equipment\n  maintenance procurement proposal only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na switch-throw, signal-clearance, or track-routing finalization\ndecision -- these are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely, not merely gated behind escalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Operator unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered operator record (`:no-operator`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the operator is.\n2. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself).\n3. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op allowlist\n   is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:op-not-allowed`).\n4. **Section basis** -- a proposal citing a section must cite a\n   REGISTERED section belonging to the proposing operator\n   (`:unknown-section` / `:section-wrong-operator`).\n5. **No switch/signal/routing finalization** -- the proposal's\n   `:action-text` must never describe throwing a track switch, clearing\n   a signal, or finalizing a track-routing decision\n   (`:finalizes-switch-or-signal`), REGARDLESS of the declared `:op`.\n   This is a hard, PERMANENT block -- there is no maturity level or\n   confidence at which this actor may auto-commit or human-approve its\n   way past this rule; it is an outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's `always-escalate-ops`). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface a switch-malfunction/signal-anomaly\n  observation -- it never resolves the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-maintenance-order` proposal whose `:maintenance-cost`\n  exceeds the CITED SECTION's registered `:max-maintenance-cost`\n  ceiling (inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-coordinate-maintenance-order-within-ceiling`) -- always needs\n  human sign-off, independent of confidence. Unlike a single global\n  constant, this ceiling is per-section registered data (mirroring the\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` reference's per-account\n  `:max-transaction-amount` ceiling shape), so different sections can\n  carry different procurement authority.\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"switch\", \"signal\", \"track\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and this vertical's domain\nvocabulary is an especially sharp case of that risk, because rail\nsections are routinely NAMED with those exact words (e.g. a section\nliterally named \"Switch 12 Junction\" or \"Signal Box 4\" -- equipment\nidentification, not a proposal to actuate it).\n`railsignalcrew.governor/finalization-patterns` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization ACTION PHRASES (verb + object -- \"throw the track\nswitch\", \"clear the signal\", \"set the route\"), never bare nouns, and\nis checked ONLY against a dedicated `:action-text` field (never against\n`:rationale` or section names, which legitimately carry switch/signal\nvocabulary as equipment identifiers).\n`railsignalcrew.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-\nself-trip` is a dedicated regression test driving the default\nmock-advisor across all four allowed ops against a section literally\nnamed \"Switch and Signal Box 4\", asserting none of them ever hard-trip\nthe finalization-scope rule. Green on first run -- the self-trip guard\nwas never actually tripped during development, precisely because the\naction-phrase design was chosen from the start rather than retrofitted\nafter a false positive.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8312\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to the\n  real repository (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8312`\n  / `cloud-itonami-isco-8312`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit, not\n  assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  8-agent retry batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 49 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/counts`\n  and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh clone of the\n  pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No mojibake in\n  the Japanese violation-detail strings (0 replacement-byte instances\n  grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-switch-throw`/\n  `:approve-signal-clearance` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops` (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a switch-throw or signal-clearance exists in\n  the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  whose failure mode is a train collision or derailment, the capability\n  itself must not exist in this actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"switch\" \"signal\"\n  \"track\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this domain's own vocabulary necessarily\n  discusses switch/signal equipment by name to do its logging/\n  scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-block the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals whenever a section happens to be named with\n  those words.\n- Scanning `:rationale` (rather than a dedicated `:action-text` field)\n  for finalization phrases: rejected -- the default advisor rationale\n  template (\"proposed <op> for operator <id> on section <id>\")\n  legitimately embeds the section-id, which can itself contain the\n  words \"switch\"/\"signal\" as an equipment identifier; scoping the\n  check to a dedicated free-text field the advisor is instructed to use\n  only for describing the proposed action keeps the check meaningful\n  without entangling it with identifier strings.\n- A single fixed global maintenance-cost threshold constant (the\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-5413` reference's shape): considered, but the\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` reference's per-account ceiling shape was\n  preferred instead, since different rail sections plausibly carry\n  different registered procurement authority in practice.\n", :adr/date "2026-07-17", :test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 49, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Railway Brake, Signal and Switch Operator Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :operator-verification :section-verification :closed-op-allowlist :maintenance-cost-threshold-escalation :switch-signal-track-routing-finalization-forbidden], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8312", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8312", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8312], :test/simulator :railsignalcrew.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8312 — Railway Brake, Signal and Switch Operators Administrative/Logistics Scheduling Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8312}]